From 5223e0b3ea7c0afed217a12a885ca04b49c5b1bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 08:45:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(prices): batched price feed with Realtime push

Server
- New price-feed edge function: started by pg_cron once a minute, loops
  ~58s fetching every open market every 3s in batched Yahoo spark requests
  (20 symbols each) plus one CoinDCX ticker call for all crypto, upserts
  quotes_cache, and broadcasts changed prices every 5s on the public
  Realtime topic "prices". Lease + heartbeat in price_feed_state, Yahoo
  429/403 backoff, per-symbol chart fallback for skipped symbols.
- refresh-quotes becomes a safety net: only refreshes rows older than 30s
  (?all=1 restores the old behaviour).
- Symbol universe moved to _shared/quote_universe.ts, now also includes
  symbols users opened recently (hot_symbols).
- Migrations: price_feed_state, hot_symbols + note_hot_symbol(), price-feed
  cron, cron history cleanup.

App
- PriceStore: subscribes to the Realtime "prices" topic while in the
  foreground; kill switch via app_flags.realtime_prices_enabled.
- MarketService answers from pushed prices first, accepts cache rows up to
  30s, batches watchlist/holdings lookups, serves the home index strip from
  the cache instead of the market-overview function, and reports browsed
  symbols to the feed.
- Trade, portfolio and stock screens redraw on each push.
- "Prices may be delayed" note (with a Live dot) on home, trade and stock.

